From: Trinity AI Agent <267220563+trinity-ai-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:13:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Controller: answer codec2 input packets, encode on the
 codec threads

Codec2toAudio() decoded the M17 data and then encoded D-Star, AMBE+2,
IMBE and USRP itself, on the codec2 thread. Two problems:

- It never called SendToReflector(), so a packet with codec_in c2_1600
  or c2_3200 was never sent back.
- The AMBE, AMBE+2 (md380 emulator) and IMBE vocoder objects are also
  used by their own threads at the same time, without a lock.

Push the decoded packet onto the ambe, swambe2, imbe and usrp queues,
as AMBEtoAudio() and the other decoders already do. Those threads
handle c2 input already, apply the configured gains, and the last one
to finish sends the reply.
---
 Controller.cpp | 20 +++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Controller.cpp b/Controller.cpp
index 3035a81..2f79a49 100644
--- a/Controller.cpp
+++ b/Controller.cpp
@@ -169,9 +169,6 @@ void CController::AudiotoCodec2(std::shared_ptr<CTranscoderPacket> packet)
 // push the packet onto both the dstar and the dmr queue.
 void CController::Codec2toAudio(std::shared_ptr<CTranscoderPacket> packet)
 {
-	uint8_t ambe[9];
-	uint8_t imbe[11];
-
 	if (packet->IsSecond())
 	{
 		if (packet->GetCodecIn() == ECodecType::c2_1600)
@@ -212,14 +209,15 @@ void CController::Codec2toAudio(std::shared_ptr<CTranscoderPacket> packet)
 			packet->SetAudioSamples(tmp, false);
 		}
 	}
-	// the only thing left is to encode the two ambe, so push the packet onto both AMBE queues
-	ambevocoder.encode_2400x1200((int16_t *)packet->GetAudioSamples(), ambe);
-	packet->SetDStarData(ambe);
-	md380_encode_fec(ambe, (int16_t *)packet->GetAudioSamples());
-	packet->SetDMRData(ambe);
-	p25vocoder.encode_4400((int16_t*)packet->GetAudioSamples(), imbe);
-	packet->SetP25Data(imbe);
-	packet->SetUSRPData((int16_t*)packet->GetAudioSamples());
+	// Hand the audio to the encoder threads, as the other decoders do.
+	// The last encoder to finish sends the reply. The old code encoded
+	// here, on the codec2 thread, at the same time as the AMBE, AMBE+2
+	// and IMBE threads used the same vocoder objects, and it never sent
+	// the reply, so a codec2 input packet was never answered.
+	ambe_queue.push(packet);
+	swambe2_queue.push(packet);
+	imbe_queue.push(packet);
+	usrp_queue.push(packet);
 }
 
 void CController::ProcessC2Thread()
